 ## Background
-This method was explored as part of the development of HexPlane, a fast representation for dynamic scenes [S1]. The authors initially attempted to model dynamic scenes by extending the query space with time using fixed basis functions, similar to positional encoding. However, they found this approach computationally infeasible and visually inferior, leading to the development of the HexPlane architecture which uses feature planes instead of a full 3D basis stack [S1]. The design is discussed in Section 9.1 of the HexPlane paper as a "Failed Design for Dynamic Scenes" [S1].
